SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pauvreté et privations de l'enfant en 2021","publisher":"UNICEF RDC","publication_date":"2021-11","url":"https://www.unicef.org/drcongo/rapports/pauvrete-privations-enfant-rdc-2021","claim":"UNICEF's 2021 child-poverty study found that 74.6% of children aged 0-17 in the DRC were multidimensionally poor and faced overlapping privations in health, nutrition, education, protection, water, sanitation, and hygiene.","locator":"lines 68-70","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UNICEF country report with explicit quantified baseline indicators and clear methodological framing.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Baseline context immediately preceding the 2022 target year; useful for judging improvement against inherited deprivation.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect baseline only; this measures inherited welfare conditions rather than Tshisekedi's own 2022 output.","contrary_evidence":["The report is a 2021 baseline and does not itself measure 2022 change or ruler-specific delivery."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"WHO Global Health Emergency Appeal: DRC","publisher":"World Health Organization","publication_date":"2022-03-07","url":"https://www.who.int/publications/m/item/who-global-health-emergency-appeal-drc","claim":"WHO reported that during vaccine responses in the DRC, 2,635,401 people were vaccinated against cholera, 162,518 people were vaccinated against meningitis, and 1,180,268 children were vaccinated against measles.","locator":"line 224","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"WHO publication with precise numerical response totals and direct country fit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and relevant to the target year's health-crisis response capacity.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the vaccination output reflects a national response environment under the Tshisekedi administration, though implementation was carried by health authorities and partners.","contrary_evidence":["The document is an appeal/summary of response activity, not a ruler-authored policy statement."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.5","6B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ebola Virus Disease - Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"World Health Organization","publication_date":"2022-09-29","url":"https://www.who.int/emergencies/disease-outbreak-news/item/2022-DON411","claim":"WHO said the North Kivu Ebola outbreak ended after no additional cases were found, and that 550 people in the affected health zone had been vaccinated using ring strategy, with frontline health workers forming most of the vaccinated group.","locator":"line 235 and outbreak summary","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct WHO outbreak bulletin with response metrics and a dated end-of-outbreak determination.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and tied to crisis response in eastern DRC.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the response was led by the national health ministry with WHO and partners under the incumbent administration.","contrary_evidence":["The bulletin credits the Ministry of Health and partners, so ruler-level attribution is indirect."],"lenses":["6B.6","6B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ebola outbreak 2022 - Equateur Province, DRC","publisher":"World Health Organization","publication_date":"2022-07-04","url":"https://www.who.int/emergencies/situations/ebola-%C3%A9quateur-province-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-2022","claim":"WHO said the Equateur Ebola outbreak was brought to an end swiftly with limited transmission because of the robust response by national authorities.","locator":"line 220","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct WHO outbreak page with a clear conclusion on response effectiveness and timing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the 2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: this is national-authority performance under Tshisekedi's government, not exclusive presidential causation.","contrary_evidence":["The page is a public-health summary and does not isolate the president's own operational decisions."],"lenses":["6B.6","6B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Des solutions locales pour lutter contre la malnutrition","publisher":"UNICEF RDC","publication_date":"2022-06-06","url":"https://www.unicef.org/drcongo/recits/solutions-locales-lutter-malnutrition","claim":"In Tanganyika, UNICEF said 300 children suffering from severe malnutrition were being treated in Manono, and that cash transfers plus nutrition counseling helped a child named Mbuyu recover weight and improve diet within three months.","locator":"lines 79-84","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UNICEF field story with concrete treatment and household-support details, though narrated through a beneficiary case.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and tied to nutrition delivery under conflict and poverty constraints.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the intervention was UNICEF-supported and partnered with Germany, but it reflects the social-protection and health-delivery environment under Tshisekedi.","contrary_evidence":["This is a localized project story and does not prove national nutrition-system performance."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.4","6B.6","6B.8","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Building schools together with communities","publisher":"UNICEF RDC","publication_date":"2022-09-02","url":"https://www.unicef.org/drcongo/en/recits/building-schools-together-with-communities","claim":"In Kasai-Central, UNICEF and villagers rebuilt Lunyenga Primary School in three months; the school was one of 22 built with community help, after more than 550 schools had been destroyed and over 100,000 students were left without classrooms.","locator":"lines 73-101","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct 2022 UNICEF account with specific reconstruction counts, timing, and student impact.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and relevant to education recovery from violence and displacement.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the rebuilding was done by UNICEF and communities, but it shows the administration's education-recovery environment and ability to enable local delivery.","contrary_evidence":["The destruction was driven by prior conflict; the article does not isolate central-government funding as the sole driver of recovery."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.4","6B.8","6B.9","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Rendre l'eau disponible dans les centres de santé","publisher":"UNICEF RDC","publication_date":"2022-03-22","url":"https://www.unicef.org/drcongo/recits/rendre-leau-disponible-dans-les-centres-de-sante","claim":"UNICEF said it installed a rainwater capture and storage system at the Sacre Coeur health centre in Walikale so the centre would have permanent water access, improve the quality of care, and protect patient dignity.","locator":"lines 73-83","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct field report with concrete infrastructure and service-quality effects in a health facility.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and relevant to health-service delivery.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the project was UNICEF-supported with BMZ/KfW, but it evidences the wider public-service environment under the incumbent government.","contrary_evidence":["This is a single facility intervention, not a systemwide health-sector audit."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.4","6B.8","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Education Cannot Wait and UNICEF with partners call for substantial increase in funding for crisis-affected children in the Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"UNICEF RDC","publication_date":"2022-10-27","url":"https://www.unicef.org/drcongo/en/press-releases/call-substantial-increase-funding-crisis-affected-children","claim":"UNICEF said the DRC had about five million internally displaced persons, including 700,000 displaced in 2022 alone, and that 3.2 million children aged 6 to 11 were out of school; the joint programme in Tanganyika was presented as a model for girls' access and post-conflict recovery.","locator":"lines 59-74","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct 2022 UNICEF press release with clear casualty/displacement and schooling figures plus a government-linked programme example.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and tightly relevant to crisis-linked education deprivation and response.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the figures largely reflect conflict and displacement pressures, but the programme operates in the national education environment under Tshisekedi.","contrary_evidence":["The main causes are conflict and displacement, so this is partly a context source rather than a pure ruler-performance measure."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.6","6B.8","6B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"An integrated response for Central African refugee populations","publisher":"UNICEF RDC","publication_date":"2022-02-16","url":"https://www.unicef.org/drcongo/en/stories/integrated-response-central-african-refugee-populations","claim":"With ECHO support, UNICEF increased access to essential basic services that directly affect the survival of Central African refugees and host populations in northern DRC, including WASH and child- and gender-based-violence protection measures.","locator":"lines 59-60 and 72-80","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct UNICEF story with explicit service-delivery claims, though much of the operational detail is narrative and donor-backed.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and relevant to vulnerable-group support and crisis service delivery.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: donor-backed local delivery is not solely presidential, but it reflects the national welfare environment and the government's ability to host and coordinate services.","contrary_evidence":["The project is externally supported and does not demonstrate nationwide government delivery by itself."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.6","6B.8","6B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Life is tough here","publisher":"UNICEF RDC","publication_date":"2022-09-12","url":"https://www.unicef.org/drcongo/en/recits/life-is-tough-here","claim":"UNICEF reported that a displaced mother in Rutshuru received emergency household items through a rapid-response distribution program, and that 4,700 other families received similar aid to improve hygiene and protect against diseases such as cholera.","locator":"lines 87-100","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct 2022 field story with named beneficiary and concrete assistance counts, though still a localized humanitarian vignette.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and tied to displacement, hygiene, and emergency protection.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the aid is partner-delivered, but it reflects the government's inability or willingness to support displaced households in the existing crisis environment.","contrary_evidence":["This is a localized emergency intervention, not a full measure of national social policy."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.6","6B.8"]}

Ledger
- Candidates found: 41
- Documents opened: 18
- Duplicate families collapsed: 13
- Irrelevant or out-of-period: 6
- Inaccessible: 2
- Accepted distinct new URLs: 10

Gaps
- Direct 2022 budget-execution, audited outcome, and ministry-level administrative statistics remain thinner than the project and humanitarian paper trail.
- Attribution is often moderate rather than exclusive because many gains came through UNICEF, WHO, WFP, World Bank, or donor-backed implementation.
- The record is strongest on crisis response, localized service delivery, and human-development baseline, and weaker on ruler-owned nationwide systems change in 2022.
- Best next sources are 2022 sector execution reports from health, education, and social affairs, plus any DHS/MICS or administrative survey releases that quantify household gains and regional inequality.

No score assigned.
